y doesn't want to play a move  you know like Bishop to d3 you know  really hampering his you know  dark-squared bishop development can't  really move his pawn for a while if he  doesn't have to his first move he really  doesn't want to be pawn to d3 if he  doesn't have to you know simply because  he is now blocking off his LightSquared  bishop development so instead he's now  going to bring his queen to a4 again be  aggressive sometimes in this case you  definitely need to be aggressive you  know again pinning down this night and  also defending this pawn here on e4 now  from here black kin he can do one of a  couple things he can bring his queen  down to d6 if he wanted to  from here white can start to you know  try to harass this Queen here on d6 he  can play Knight to a3 getting ready for  his knight to come to b5 black can now  start to put more pressure  he can play Knight to f6 again really  starting to attack this pawn here on e4  white now has to play and Knight to b5  trying to distract this Queen on d6  after the Queen moves and now you know  white can play pawn to d3 so again you  know from here white can always bring  his Bishop to e2 castle on the King side  if he wants to he's a little bit weak in  his pawn structure but he can still have  a very very good game from here now if  we come back a few moves I'll just go  through them again after d5 here and the  Queen comes to f4 now the bishop can  also come to d7 you may not see the  Queen come down to d6 a lot of people  like to deal with you know a pin down  Knight which is bringing their Bishop  down to D 7 so if you do see this  instead we can now just play pawn takes  on d5 now it does get very very crazy  because black can now play Knight to d4  so this is a very very aggressive line  from black as you can see he's hanging  his knight here on the 4  but he's also has a discovered attack  with you know his Bishop Iran d7 on this  Queen here on a5 so again very very  aggressive line from black this i